  "body": "Stacked on #3353 (merge #3353 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n2D Pocket gets the shared \"Pass starts at\" option of #3316 (Auto / Inside / Outside).\n\n- `OpParams::Pocket` gets the field `pass_start: machining2d::PassStart`. This is the same type as on 2D Offset. There is no new type.\n- The project file uses the same key, `pass_start`. The file never writes `auto`. Files without the key read as Auto.\n- The Passes tab of 2D Pocket shows the same row, `Pass starts at` (`pass_start_row`).\n- MCP uses the same generic `edit_operation` door. Undo goes through `EditOperationParams`.\n- The digest writes the value only off Auto. The byte pair is now one helper, `digest::write_pass_start`. 2D Offset and 2D Pocket both use it.\n- The generator calls `pocket_started` (from #3353) instead of `pocket_entered_with_relief`. On Auto, the two functions are byte-identical.\n- Waterline and Offset rings read the value through the #3316 ring law (`PassStart::rank`).\n- Zigzag rows have no inside or outside. With Inside or Outside, the planner adds the path note `PASS_START_ZIGZAG_NOTE`.\n- Rest machining keeps its own order of the rest areas. With Inside or Outside, the generator adds the path note `PASS_START_REST_NOTE`.\n- About 40 test struct literals get `pass_start: Default::default()`. This is a mechanical change.\n- The site guide (2D Pocket) gets a row and a paragraph.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3354-pocket-pass-start.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n2D Pocket had no pass-order choice. With an Outside containment, the ring strategies cut each level core-first. The first ring was then a full slot in the stock. This is the #3316 defect on the pocket kind.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe pins (`crates/app/tests/pocket_pass_start.rs`, `fig8.step`, EM-0800-4FL, Outside containment, the #3316 heights):\n\n- `fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge`: Waterline and Offset rings. The first ring of each level is at least one tool radius outside the stock. The last ring is on the part wall.\n- `fig8_pocket_inside_starts_each_level_on_the_part_wall`\n- `fig8_pocket_auto_keeps_the_core_first_order`: Auto has no note and no stock-edge start.\n- `fig8_zigzag_pocket_says_pass_start_is_not_used`\n- `fig8_rest_pocket_says_pass_start_is_not_used`\n- `pocket_pass_start_rides_mcp_undo_and_the_file`: an unknown word is refused, `auto` is not written, undo restores the value, and the file round-trips.\n- `operation::rest_op_tests::pass_start_moves_the_pocket_stamp_only_off_auto` (app lib)\n- `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_pocket_passes_tab_offers_pass_start_and_shows_the_draft` (ui lib)\n\nMutation checks. I removed each guard, ran its pin, and put the guard back. Each pin went red and then green again:\n\n- generator call back to `pocket_entered_with_relief`: the Outside, Inside and Zigzag pins went red.\n- Zigzag note removed: the Zigzag pin went red.\n- file DTO writes Auto always: the MCP and file pin went red.\n- digest bytes removed: the stamp pin went red.\n- rest note removed: the rest pin went red.\n- UI row removed: the UI pin went red.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base base-3353` planned 743 steps, because any change in `crates/app/src` selects every app suite. That run hit its time limit, so I ran a targeted set instead.\n- Green: app lib, motion lib and ui lib.\n- Green: every test binary that this PR edits (35 app suites and `edge_loop_pick`).\n- Green: `offset_pass_start`, `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`, `conformance`, `whole_model_pocket`, `mcp_dxf` and `do_not_touch`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes. Auto is byte-identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick gate (743 steps) did not complete. See the Gate list above for what ran.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) were not run.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row still says \"2D Offset\" only. The edit needed a permission that this headless run did not have. A follow-up can add \"or a 2D Pocket\" and the note about Zigzag and rest.\n- Pass start with \"Do not touch\" (`pocket_avoid_started`) is not wired for 2D Pocket. 2D Pocket does not use the avoid planner.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #3353 (the shared type, key, row and ring law). This PR changes one line of #3353 in `params/mill2d.rs`, because the Offset2D digest now uses the shared helper. The bytes are the same.\n- Other open PRs touch `generate.rs`, `project/params.rs` and `params_impl.rs` (#3283, #3251, #3103, #3058, #2890, #2831) and `mill2d_page.rs` (#2817, #2890). They change different functions or arms. The PR that merges second does the refresh.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket: new \"Pass starts at\" option (Auto / Inside / Outside) on the Passes tab, in MCP and in the project file; Outside starts each ring level at the outer edge, so an Outside containment no longer slots the stock.\n\nFixes #3354\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
